Serialize every libfabric endpoint, CQ and AV call on a rail.

NIXL 1.5.0's libfabric rails open their domains with FI_THREAD_COMPLETION,
under which the provider takes no locks on the endpoint, the completion
queue or the address vector and the application must serialize them. The
progress thread posts descriptors in drainPostQueue() and reads the CQ in
pollForCompletions() without holding ep_mutex_, while caller threads post
control messages through postSend() holding it, so both paths race.

Take ep_mutex_ around the fi_* calls that were missing it, release it
before running completion callbacks, and document the two rules the lock
follows: hold it only around the call itself, never around an FI_EAGAIN
retry loop, and keep it innermost.

This is a backport of ai-dynamo/nixl#2308, merged upstream after v1.5.0 as
2c1f6eff71. The diff is that merge's, unchanged.

TODO(GEX-4323): drop once the fix ships in a tagged NIXL release.

